   2. **System Building** – The agent will invoke `build_simulation_system` with `protein_file` pointing to `protein_clean.pdb`. The tool will automatically detect the ligand topology in the same directory, merge the protein and ligand coordinates into a single GRO file, generate the amber99sb-ildn topology (`system.top`), and create a cubic TIP3P box with a 1.2 nm buffer.  
   3. **Solvation and Ion Addition** – `build_simulation_system` will also add TIP3P water molecules and neutralize the system with Na⁺/Cl⁻ ions. It will then add additional ions to reach a 0.15 M NaCl concentration, as per the default simulation conditions.  
   4. **MDP Generation** – The tool will produce a set of MDP files for equilibration (NVT, NPT) and a production run. The agent will then create two copies of the production MDP file, modifying the `gen_seed` parameter in each to distinct values (e.g., 12345 and 67890). This ensures two independent replicates.  
   5. **TPR and Index Files** – `build_simulation_system` will generate a TPR file (`production.tpr`) and an index file (`index.ndx`). The agent will copy these files into the working directory.  
   6. **File Organization** – All generated files – topology (`system.top`), coordinates (`system.gro`), ligand topology (`ATP.itp`), MDP files (`equil_NVT.mdp`, `equil_NPT.mdp`, `production_seed12345.mdp`, `production_seed67890.mdp`), TPR (`production.tpr`), and index (`index.ndx`) – will be placed in `/home/akp66103/workspace/agenticAI/campaigns/robustness/campaigns/pseudokin_10x2/run_01/q9y243_ATP`.  
   7. **Verification** – The agent will run a quick `gmx check` on the final GRO and TPR files to confirm that the system is ready for simulation. Any errors will be reported.

